    <p class="note">Measured 2026-10-24 on the maintainer's machine with Node.js 24.14.0 against souls 0.3.0: size of the published dist/index.js at gzip -9, median of 11 cold imports, tests and coverage from the v0.3.0 tag. The replay above was re-run against the same release on that day and gave the same output.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="binaries" class="sec binaries" aria-labelledby="binaries-title">
    <h2 id="binaries-title">Install the release binary</h2>
    <p class="intro">The default way to run <code>ghostpaw-souls</code>: one executable per platform with Node.js inside, with the same commands and the same MCP server as the npm package. Each line downloads the latest release, checks it against the release&#39;s SHA256SUMS and puts the binary on the PATH (<code>~/.local/bin</code>; the Windows script adds its folder to the user PATH). The default lines never edit <code>~/.profile</code>: <code>export PATH</code> lasts for the current shell only; the labelled <code>~/.profile</code> line keeps it for new shells. Pin a release with <code>--version &lt;x.y.z&gt;</code>; set <code>GHOSTPAW_NO_MODIFY_PATH=1</code> to keep the Windows script from changing the user PATH.</p>
    <div class="bin-cmds">
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-linux-x64-label">linux-x64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-linux-x64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-linux-x64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/souls/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target linux-x64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-linux-x64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-linux-arm64-label">linux-arm64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-linux-arm64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-linux-arm64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/souls/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target linux-arm64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-linux-arm64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-darwin-arm64-label">darwin-arm64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-darwin-arm64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-darwin-arm64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/souls/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target darwin-arm64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-darwin-arm64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-darwin-x64-label">darwin-x64</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-darwin-x64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-darwin-x64-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/souls/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target darwin-x64 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-darwin-x64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-windows-x64-label">windows-x64 (PowerShell)</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-windows-x64" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-windows-x64-label" spellcheck="false">irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/souls/main/install.ps1 | iex</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-windows-x64">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-pinned-label">linux-x64 pinned to 0.4.3</p>
        <div class="cmd"><textarea id="bin-pinned" readonly rows="2" aria-labelledby="bin-pinned-label" spellcheck="false">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GhostPawJS/souls/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --target linux-x64 --version 0.4.3 &amp;&amp; export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;</textarea><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="bin-pinned">Copy</button></div></div>
        <div><p class="cmd-label" id="bin-profile-label">linux-x64, also adding ~/.local/bin to ~/.profile (edits that file once)</p>
